{1 tiny_languages }

Languages as text, parsed and run, written from scratch for teaching:
one library per language, each interface with its grammar, a worked
example and its references. None of them knows the
{{:../elm_playground/index.html} Elm Playground}: what a program can
touch outside itself is a host, a record of functions its caller gives
(a sheet's cells, a page's elements). They stand on
{{:../tiny_libs/index.html} tiny_libs}.

Each is a library of its own, named [tiny_languages.<name>] outside this
repository, for example in a dune file:

{v
(executable
 (name main)
 (libraries tiny_languages.scheme tiny_languages.lang_html))
v}

The libraries are unwrapped: their modules are used by their own names,
[Scheme_eval], [Html_tree].

{2:formula The spreadsheet's formulas}

[tiny_languages.formula]: arithmetic over numbers and cells, SUM and its
kin over ranges; recursive descent, the parser to know first.

{!modules: Formula}

{2:basic BASIC}

[tiny_languages.basic]: Tiny BASIC, Integer BASIC and Applesoft; a
program run as a {{:../tiny_libs/Talk/index.html}Talk} conversation.

{!modules: Basic_parse Basic_run Basic_session Basic_disk}

{2:lisps The Lisps}

s-expressions, the syntax they share ([tiny_languages.sexpr]), a small
Emacs Lisp ([tiny_languages.lisp]), a small Scheme and HtDP's Beginning
Student, run by a CESK machine, with its stepper
([tiny_languages.scheme]):

{!modules:
    Sexpr Sexpr_read
    Lisp Lisp_read Lisp_eval Lisp_prelude
    Scheme Scheme_image Scheme_syntax Scheme_prims Scheme_prelude
    Scheme_eval Scheme_step
}

{2:pascal Pascal}

[tiny_languages.pascal]: compiled in one pass to P-code and run on a
P-machine, with its debugger.

{!modules: Pascal_lexer Pascal_compile Pcode Pmachine Pdebug Pascal_disk}

{2:hypertalk HyperTalk}

[tiny_languages.hypertalk]: HyperCard's language, the cards the host's.

{!modules: Hypertalk}

{2:smalltalk Smalltalk-80}

[tiny_languages.smalltalk]: from the Blue Book, compiled to its bytecodes
and run by its interpreter over an object table, its kernel classes in
Smalltalk bootstrapped from their text.

{!modules:
    St_lexer St_ast St_parse St_chunk St_memory St_class St_bytecode
    St_compile St_interp St_primitives St_kernel St_boot St_debug
    St_image St_bitblt
}

{2:scratch Scratch and Snap!}

[tiny_languages.scratch]: the blocks as one table of specs, their text,
a project run as green threads.

{!modules: Scratch_blocks Scratch_text Scratch_run}

{2:postscript PostScript}

[tiny_languages.postscript]: a page described as a program; the letters
are the host's.

{!modules: Ps_lexer Ps_graphics Ps_machine Ps_disk}

{2:web The web: JavaScript, HTML, CSS}

A small JavaScript ([tiny_languages.javascript]), HTML read
([tiny_languages.lang_html]), what a page's elements look like, the
cascade and computed styles ([tiny_languages.lang_css]):

{!modules:
    Js_lexer Js_ast Js_parse Js_value Js_eval Js_builtins Js_regexp
    Charset Entities Html_lexer Dom Dtd Html_tree Line_mode Forms
    Looks Css_syntax Selectors Css Css_values Cascade Computed Ua_sheet
}

{2:config JSON and jsonnet}

[tiny_languages.lang_json] (over JavaScript's lexer) and
[tiny_languages.lang_jsonnet], for configuration files:

{!modules: Json Jsonnet Jsonnet_lexer Jsonnet_ast Jsonnet_parse}

{2:code Code read, not run}

OCaml ([tiny_languages.lang_ocaml]), C ([tiny_languages.lang_c]) and
assembly ([tiny_languages.lang_asm]), read for a code visualizer, their
tokens coloured by
{{:../tiny_libs/Highlight_code/index.html}Highlight_code}'s categories:

{!modules:
    Token_ml Lexer_ml Ast_ml Parse_ml Highlight_ml
    Token_c Lexer_c Ast_c Parse_c Highlight_c
    Highlight_asm
}
